  "question": {
    "text": "The point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lies in the angle between the lines <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> containing the origin. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> is an integer, then the sum of all possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> is"
